+// Walks the stack of the thread that `pointers` belongs to, which waits in the exception filter
+// below the frames walked. A stack overflow is usually deep recursion: the innermost frames show
+// the recursing code, the outermost ones where it was entered from.
+void Walk(const EXCEPTION_POINTERS& pointers, StackWalk& walk) {
